{
  "sn4.25:0.1": "Linked Discourses 4.25 ",
  "sn4.25:0.2": "3. Māra ",
  "sn4.25:0.3": "Māra’s Daughters ",
  "sn4.25:1.1": "And then Māra the Wicked, after reciting these verses of disillusionment in the Buddha’s presence, left that place. He sat cross-legged on the ground not far from the Buddha, silent, dismayed, shoulders drooping, downcast, depressed, with nothing to say, scratching the ground with a stick. ",
  "sn4.25:1.2": "Then Māra’s daughters Craving, Malignancy, and Lust went up to Māra the Wicked, and addressed him in verse: ",
  "sn4.25:2.1": "“Why so downhearted, dad? ",
  "sn4.25:2.2": "What man are you upset about? ",
  "sn4.25:2.3": "We’ll catch him with the snare of lust, ",
  "sn4.25:2.4": "like an elephant in the wild. ",
  "sn4.25:2.5": "We’ll tie him up and bring him back—",
  "sn4.25:2.6": "he’ll fall under your sway!” ",
  "sn4.25:3.1": "“In this world he is the perfected one, the Holy One. ",
  "sn4.25:3.2": "He’s not easily seduced by lust. ",
  "sn4.25:3.3": "He has slipped free of Māra’s dominion; ",
  "sn4.25:3.4": "that’s why I’m so upset.” ",
  "sn4.25:4.1": "Then Māra’s daughters Craving, Malignancy, and Lust went up to the Buddha, and said to him, ",
  "sn4.25:4.2": "“We serve at your feet, ascetic.” ",
  "sn4.25:4.3": "But the Buddha ignored them, since he was freed with the supreme ending of attachments. ",
  "sn4.25:5.1": "Then Craving, Malignancy, and Lust withdrew to one side to think up a plan. ",
